{
  "v": 1,
  "label": "demo recipe",
  "synthetic": true,
  "about": "Demo starter recipes for the example '3 Pepperoni Pizza + 2 Chicken Fried Rice + 3 chicken briyani + 7 mango milkshakes in 2 weeks', and the breakfasts, lunches and dinners the meal plan wizard offers for each diet, made only of products in products.json. Written for the demo: the quantities are demo house amounts, not from a published recipe, and every surface shows them as 'demo recipe'.",
  "aliases_note": "`aliases` are whole alternative names matched at the alias step; `token_aliases` map one recipe-title token to misspellings of it. Plurals are also handled by the singularise rule; the plural aliases are listed so the alias step alone covers the example sentence.",
  "diets_note": "`slot` is where a recipe is offered; `diets` lists which of vegan, vegetarian and pescatarian it satisfies and `contains` the contains-tags of the products its lines resolve to in demo mode, a seafood product's meat tag read as fish, and what the lines' own names say (a White Chocolate line is dairy whatever its product's tags) (mealplan/diets.py). `library_meta` says the same of the library recipes, whose recipes.json pantry-db shares byte for byte. tests/test_mealplan_seeds.py checks every entry against those products and names.",
  "image_note": "`image_wiki` is the English Wikipedia article whose lead image shows the dish, or the closest dish there is a picture of: the console shows that image through the demo hub (GET /hub/images/wiki?title=), credited to Wikipedia and linked back. Only the title is kept here, never an image. Checked by hand against Wikipedia's API on 2026-10-10 (each title is an article with a lead image); the tests never call Wikipedia.",
  "needs_demo_products": {
    "Instant Yeast": 169,
    "Pepperoni": 167,
    "Frozen Mango": 166
  },
